DESCRIPTION:This listing is for a three session Beginner Knitting Course. 
 The classes will be held in person at Bistitchual on Saturday November 14t
 h\, 21st and 28th from 2:30-4:00pm Have you always wanted to learn to knit
 ? We’ve got you covered! Beginner Knitting is a course for brand new beg
 inners\, and over these three 1.5hr classes\, Mike will teach you everythi
 ng you need to create a basic project from beginning to end. Our class siz
 e is capped at 4 people\, so everyone can receive the attention they need.
  Mike will share lots of tips and techniques to get you well on your way. 
 (No experience necessary) Materials: Yarn and needles will be provided. Wh
 at We’ll Learn - How to make a slip knot. - Casting on. - The Knit stitc
 h. - The Purl stitch. - Exploring Knit / Purl combinations. - Binding off.
  - Weaving in ends. - Fixing common mistakes and how to avoid them. - Comm
 on uses of flat knitting. - Intro into Ravelry. Please note that classes w
 ill only proceed if we have a minimum of two attendees . If the minimum is
  not met\, there will be the option for a refund or to reschedule. There w
 ill be a four person maximum for each class. Please pre-book your spot to 
 let us know you are coming! About the instructor : Tired of disposing of c
 lothes that were still perfectly wearable\, Mike (he/him) started crafting
  mainly as a means of mending and repair. This led him to knitting (and la
 ter crochet)\, which pretty much immediately became one of his favourite t
 ools of self-expression. Cancellation Policy Classes must be paid for at t
 he time of registration to reserve your spot. - If cancelled 48 hrs or mor
 e prior to the start of the first class will be given a store credit. Clas
 ses cancelled less than 48 hrs prior to the start of the class will not be
  reimbursed.
